>> title: Patty Melt
>> category: Sandwiches & Rolls
>> tags: beef, rye, onion, griddle, lunch
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: patty melt, patty melt sandwich, rye burger
>> servings: 2
>> time: 55 min
>> step.1: cook the onions down 35 min, low and slow
>> step.2: griddle the thin patties 4 min
>> step.3: layer on rye, cheese against both slices
>> step.4: griddle the whole sandwich 6 min, both faces

Cook @yellow onions{2%large}(sliced thin) in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g) over medium-low heat ~fry{35%min}, stirring every few minutes, until they collapse to a third and go the colour of a penny.

Griddle @ground beef{10%oz}(280 g; 80/20 chuck, pressed into two thin oblongs the shape of the bread) seasoned with @kosher salt{1/2%tsp}(3 g) and @coarse black pepper{1/2%tsp}(1 g) ~sear{4%min}, turning once.

Layer @rye bread{4%slices} with @swiss cheese{4%slices} against both inside faces, @&(~2)cooked onions{} and @&(~1)patties{} in the middle.

Griddle @&(~1)built sandwiches{} in @unsalted butter{2%Tbs}(28 g) over medium-low heat ~fry{6%min}, turning once and pressing lightly, until both faces are dark gold and the cheese runs at the edges.
